From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 16:47:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Catch git permission denied errors and raise a user-friendly
 GitPermissionError

When a deploy key lacks write access, git push (and other git
operations) fail with a raw GitPython GitCommandError like:

  Cmd('git') failed due to: exit code(128)
    cmdline: git push origin pb-test-2
    stderr: 'ERROR: Permission to Zenlytic/dev-demo-data-model.git denied to deploy key ...'

This surfaces the raw dump to the user on actions like Save Model.
Translate these failures into GitPermissionError (a subclass of
MetricsLayerException) with a message that is safe to display to
the user. Non-permission git errors propagate unchanged.

Fixes ZEN-8504
